From: Rafal Chlodnicki <rchl2k@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:10:40 +0200
Subject: Fix hdr_histogram build with Clang 22 on Windows x64

ClangCL 22 (Visual Studio 2026) treats -Wincompatible-pointer-types as an
error. count_leading_zeros_64() passed a uint32_t* to _BitScanReverse64(),
which takes an unsigned long*.

Matches the fix in HdrHistogram_c 0.12.0, which Node.js picked up in
https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/1271bb448a. Drop this patch once
the Node.js version being built includes histogram 0.12.0.

diff --git a/deps/histogram/src/hdr_histogram.c b/deps/histogram/src/hdr_histogram.c
index a34de2c1b2132ddcbe73220e694b97f78514f7d8..23c711a17142c3ccaf620a6b2246d884b7639954 100644
--- a/deps/histogram/src/hdr_histogram.c
+++ b/deps/histogram/src/hdr_histogram.c
@@ -187,7 +187,8 @@ static int64_t power(int64_t base, int64_t exp)
 static int32_t count_leading_zeros_64(int64_t value)
 {
 #if defined(_MSC_VER) && !(defined(__clang__) && (defined(_M_ARM) || defined(_M_ARM64)))
-    uint32_t leading_zero = 0;
+    /* _BitScanReverse writes an unsigned long */
+    unsigned long leading_zero = 0;
 #if defined(_WIN64)
     _BitScanReverse64(&leading_zero, value);
 #else
